--- fixed implementation boundary ---
The input libraries are pure C and export GetTLS, SetTLS, and ResetTLS over a common C ABI.
The four actual inputs are libtls-ie.so, libtls-gd.so, libtls-desc.so, and the naturally available non-gating libtls-ld.so.
Host GCC 14.2.0 only compiles freestanding x86_64 PIC objects so the classic gnu and gnu2 TLS dialects are explicit; fixed API 24 OHOS clang/lld links every final shared object.
Every final link uses --no-relax; final readelf and llvm-objdump results below, rather than compiler flags, determine the measured TLS model.
No Go command, Go source, NetBird source, WireGuard source, SDK source, patched toolchain, Native Child API, fork, exec, TUN, DNS, public network, or product path is used.
The pure-C build removes historical ignored libgoprobe.so, libneededprobe.so, and libtlsprobe.so from the HAP input directory before producing the four current inputs.
The Node-API harness creates and confirms a waiting pthread before each dlopen; after successful dlopen it releases that thread to resolve GetTLS/SetTLS/ResetTLS and creates a second pthread after dlopen to resolve the same ABI.
For every dynamic model, main, pre-dlopen, and post-dlopen threads must each observe initial 42, use distinct values for 100 SetTLS/GetTLS cycles, and ResetTLS back to 42.
The initial-exec control must reproduce the EV-R1-EMU24-20260717-0007 late RTLD_NOW|RTLD_LOCAL loader rejection before any dynamic model runs; an unexpected IE load is environment drift and stops the suite.
Tier1 PASS requires classic GD or TLSDESC to pass; local-dynamic is measured but non-gating.

