$ readelf -lWrdsW libtls-ie.so; llvm-objdump -dr --no-show-raw-insn libtls-ie.so
ELF64 x86-64 ET_DYN; SONAME libtls-ie.so; PT_TLS filesz=4 memsz=4 align=4; FLAGS BIND_NOW STATIC_TLS; FLAGS_1 NOW.
.rela.dyn contains R_X86_64_TPOFF64 for tls_probe_value; no DTPMOD64, DTPOFF64, TLSDESC, or __tls_get_addr.
Dynamic exports are GetTLS, SetTLS, ResetTLS, and tls_probe_value.
GetTLS loads a relocated offset then executes movl %fs:(%rax), %eax; SetTLS and ResetTLS use the same direct %fs model.
IE_MODEL=INITIAL_EXEC_CONFIRMED

$ readelf -lWrdsW libtls-gd.so; llvm-objdump -dr --no-show-raw-insn libtls-gd.so
ELF64 x86-64 ET_DYN; SONAME libtls-gd.so; PT_TLS filesz=4 memsz=4 align=4; FLAGS BIND_NOW; FLAGS_1 NOW; STATIC_TLS absent.
.rela.dyn contains R_X86_64_DTPMOD64 and R_X86_64_DTPOFF64 for tls_probe_value; .rela.plt contains R_X86_64_JUMP_SLOT for undefined __tls_get_addr; TPOFF and TLSDESC are absent.
GetTLS, SetTLS, and ResetTLS each load the GD descriptor address and call __tls_get_addr@plt before accessing the returned address.
