--- interpretation boundary ---
The exact API 24 x86_64 TestRunner loader rejects a real initial-exec TLS late load but accepts verified classic GD, TLSDESC gnu2, and local-dynamic inputs while preserving per-thread initializers and isolation for threads created both before and after dlopen.
Tier1 therefore passes because both gating dynamic models pass; the API24 x86_64 tuple is not stopped by this gate.
This does not show that Go 1.25.12 emits or supports either accepted model, does not validate an unmerged upstream change, and does not authorize or implement a Go/runtime/toolchain patch.
The next gate is a separately bounded Tier2 Go/toolchain feasibility decision using the still-unmerged upstream work only as reference; no Tier2 implementation starts from this record alone.
The result does not generalize to arm64, a named physical device, commercial Huawei HarmonyOS, another loader or image, Go runtime, NetBird, VPN, product support, signing, channel acceptance, or stage exit.
The result does not reverse or exit R0, R1, or R2; upstream patch count remains zero.
